# Manual REST Client requests for /locations (VS Code REST Client).
# Sign in with an approved review account of REVIEW_ACCOUNTS in apps/backend/.env: set the email and code below.
# Codes are read from the backend log when RESEND_API_KEY is unset.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = admin@example.com
@code = 345678

### Request a sign-in code (expects 202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "locale": "pt-BR"
}

### Sign in (expects 200 with accessToken)
# @name session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

###
@token = {{session.response.body.accessToken}}

### List the active locations, sorted by name ignoring case and accents (expects 200 with { items: [{ id, name, address, latitude, longitude, upcomingClasses }] }; any approved account)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a location (expects 201 with { id, name, address, latitude, longitude, upcomingClasses: 0 }; admins only)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Praia do Futuro",
  "address": "Av. Zezé Diogo, 5000 – Fortaleza",
  "latitude": -3.7442,
  "longitude": -38.4617
}

###
@locationId = {{created.response.body.id}}

### The same name ignoring case and accents (expects 409 location.name.duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "práia do futuro",
  "address": "Outro endereço",
  "latitude": -3.7,
  "longitude": -38.5
}

### Empty name and address, no point (expects 422 with errors location.name.required, location.address.required and location.point.required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "address": ""
}

### Without a token (expects 401 auth.token.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations

### As a student or instructor (expects 403 user.role.notAdmin on POST): use that account's token
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Outro local",
  "address": "Rua A",
  "latitude": -3.7,
  "longitude": -38.5
}

### A point out of range (expects 422 location.point.invalid)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fora do mapa",
  "address": "Rua A",
  "latitude": 91,
  "longitude": -38.5
}

### Edit a location; it applies to every class that uses it. notify: true tells the instructors of its upcoming classes (expects 200 with the location; admins only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/locations/{{locationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Praia do Futuro",
  "address": "Av. Zezé Diogo, 5100 – Fortaleza",
  "latitude": -3.7445,
  "longitude": -38.4615,
  "notify": true
}

### Remove (archive) a location: it leaves the list, its name is freed, its classes keep it (expects 204; again: 409 location.archived)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locations/{{locationId}}/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Address suggestions from Google Places (expects 200 with { items: [{ placeId, title, description }] }, empty without GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY; admins only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations/address-suggestions?q=praia%20do%20fut&sessionToken=abc123&language=pt-BR
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The place behind a suggestion (expects 200 with { address, latitude, longitude, name }; 404 location.place.notFound when unknown)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locations/address-suggestions/PLACE_ID?sessionToken=abc123&language=pt-BR
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
